Package: alloy
Type: Package
Title: Unified Modeling Framework for Regression and Classification
Version: 0.0.0.916
Authors@R: c(
  person("Andri", "Signorell", email = "andri@signorell.net", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Fits regression and classification models of very different
    origins through one interface. A single call to fitMod() covers
    linear, generalised linear, ordinal, robust, censored, mixed and
    survival models as well as trees, random forests, boosting,
    penalised regression, support vector machines and neural networks,
    and it selects a sensible method automatically from the type of the
    response. Fitted objects carry a common class, so printing,
    prediction and plotting behave the same way whatever was fitted
    underneath, and coefficient tables can be reported on the odds
    ratio, rate ratio, hazard ratio or time ratio scale. A set of
    diagnostics for binary responses complements the model fitting,
    among them binned residuals, calibration curves, randomised quantile
    residuals, influence and separation plots.
